      "key": "release_authority_and_result_boundaries",
      "statement": "A mutable workspace has no fixed identity and is not called a Product. An install used as builder substrate is bound as a development product and transfers no meaning or authority to the authored Product; a product definition is a source-project surface, not the released artifact. Shared carriers, names and paths grant no membership. Release handling follows intake triage, and an open release window permits no untriaged change. Release process owns neither Product meaning nor adoption; operation outcome is not acceptance. Refusal, stopping, fail-closed operation, invalid state and failed checks report in the core and are never success.",
